  "analysis": "Both responses address the core requirements (timeout, fail‑open fallback, rate‑limit protection, manual‑review routing, dual approval, audit‑log immutability). MJL offers a very granular G‑stage process but insists on running the full 45‑minute regression suite before release, which could jeopardize the tight deadline. NVJ provides a concise, actionable lane‑based plan, includes targeted tests, a canary rollout, and only runs the full suite if necessary, better aligning with the cost and time constraints.",
